  "finding": "Fresh 31 October 2026 inspection of the public OSIRIS examination programme ECTRIE/FEWBA26ECTRI establishes the 2026 entrant pathway: 60+60+60 EC. This controls over historical transition tables, the prior-year ESE/EFR guide and the public 2027–2028 preview. Econometrics is selected under the neutral broad-identity rule, independently of UCR fit. The 20-EC major is Advanced Econometrics4, one restricted methods course4 (Quantitative Methods for Data Science selected) and one seminar12 (Seminar in Forecasting selected). Career Skills2 is split into mandatory Your Future Career1 and an offered Job Market Skills1 choice. Genuine minor12 and remaining electives12 are preserved. Thesis10 is a compulsory award requirement under OER Arts10–12; the catalogue retains an older administrative thesis registration record, which is not treated as a new offered2026 course or an omitted requirement. Programme-specific guidance is non-credit. Current course descriptions confirm the foundations and prerequisite chain; Ethics precedes the major seminar, which precedes the individual major-linked thesis. All years1–2 completed before the seminar.",
  "neutralSelection": "Econometrics retains the broad core; within it choose the general economic forecasting seminar and Data Science methods option rather than the domain-specific finance option, independently of the UCR alternatives. Advanced4+methods4+seminar12=20; thesis10 separate. No duplicated parent20 plus child20. Year1=60,year2=60,year3=12minor+12electives+1career+1career+4ethics+4advanced+4methods+12seminar+10thesis=60. All35 components total180. Genuine24profiling space retains permitted minor branch; other internship/exchange branches not added. Catalogue’s older thesis administrative registration remains identified internally; current formal award rule and10EC programme requirement govern, not an invented current course offering.",
  "progression": "Complete firsttwo years and their foundations first; Academic Skills concurrent with introductory Case Studies; Ethics after both, then Advanced Econometrics and its Econometrics2/TimeSeries foundations before Forecasting seminar. Quantitative Methods for Data Science follows Econometrics2, Markov and Marketing. At least96EC at start for Career Skills; core and chosen job-market week respected. Thesis only after seminar passed. Year1practical70% attendance except programming exemption, zeroEC guidance100%, major seminar100%, thesis individual/major-linked/deadline as OER. No inconsistent minor/major alternatives combined.",
  "conflictResolution": "2026 public examination programme controls current component membership over the historical ECTRIE16ECTRICS archived seminar,2025–26 ESE/EFR guide’s generic three-course statement and public2027–28preview. No reliance on closed MyEUR, authentication, or third-party notes. Public API responses were retrieved without a browser or account."
